==English==

===Etymology===
Random House Unabridged Dictionary: shortened from ''gooney'', from obsolete ''gony'' of unknown origin, for "[[simpleton]]" The meaning of "hired thug" is influenced by the comic strip character [[w:Alice the Goon]]

===Pronunciation===
*Rhymes: [[Rhymes:English:-uːn|-uːn]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[thug]], a usually muscular henchman with very little intelligence (also known as a 'Hired Goon'). The term ''goon'' rose to prominence in this context thanks to frequent usage in [[Popeye]].
# A [[fool]], or someone considered slightly [[silly]] or outlandish. This is likely due to the popular radio show, "The Goon Show" starring Spike Milligan and Peter Sellers.
# A [[beauty], usually a person that's appealing to the eye; or someone who has great taste in clothes. 
